<div xmlns:i18n="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/i18n"
     xmlns:tal="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/tal"
     class="report-problem-viewlet"
     i18n:domain="imio.reportproblem"
>

  <!-- Minimal on purpose, so that a site can override it through z3c.jbot.

     No <i> icon element here: plonetheme.deliberations injects its own icon
     through a CSS "::before" rule on ".report-problem-link", guarded by
     ":has(i)" so that it stands down for markup shipping an icon of its own.
     A generic add-on must not hard-code another package's icon font.

     Whether this renders at all is decided in Python, in the viewlet's
     "render": an override of this template cannot open what the guard rails
     close.

     "class" carries "pat-plone-modal" in modal mode and not in page mode, and
     that is the whole of the difference between the two modes, the href being
     the same either way. A "pat-plone-modal" link whose pattern does not
     initialise stays an ordinary link, so page mode is also the no-JavaScript
     fallback.

     "data-pat-plone-modal" is emitted in modal mode only, and its
     "actionOptions.redirectOnResponse" is load bearing: the form redirects to
     the content with a status message on success, and mockup's defaults would
     follow that redirect over AJAX and redraw the modal from the content page,
     where "#report-problem-form" no longer exists, leaving an empty modal and
     a confirmation nobody ever sees. Do not "simplify" it away.

     The label is translated in the viewlet rather than here, because the same
     string is also the aria-label: the accessible name never drifts from what
     is displayed. -->
  <a class="report-problem-link"
     tal:attributes="
       class view/link_class;
       href view/link_url;
       aria-label view/label;
       data-pat-plone-modal view/modal_options;
     "
  ><span tal:content="view/label">Report a problem</span></a>

</div>
